    "# COMPLETE TIME SERIES ROADMAP FOR CRYPTOCURRENCY PREDICTION: FROM SCRATCH TO ADVANCED\n",
    "\n",
    "## Phase 1: Foundations (Weeks 1-4)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 1-2: Python & Data Manipulation Basics\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to Learn:**\n",
    "- NumPy for numerical operations and array handling[1][2]\n",
    "- Pandas for time series data manipulation (datetime indexing, resampling, grouping)[2][3]\n",
    "- Matplotlib and Seaborn for data visualization[3][2]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Practice Tasks:**\n",
    "- Load cryptocurrency price data from APIs (Yahoo Finance, Binance, CoinGecko)[4][5][6]\n",
    "- Create datetime indices and handle missing values in time series data[7][2]\n",
    "- Plot price trends, volume charts, and candlestick patterns[8][3]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Concepts:**\n",
    "- Time series indexing with `.loc[]` and `.iloc[]`[3]\n",
    "- Resampling data (daily to weekly, hourly to daily)[2][3]\n",
    "- Handling missing timestamps and forward/backward filling[9][10]\n",
    "\n",
    "***\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 3-4: Statistical Foundations\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to Learn:**\n",
    "- Descriptive statistics (mean, median, standard deviation, skewness, kurtosis)[7][2]\n",
    "- Probability distributions and hypothesis testing[2]\n",
    "- Correlation and autocorrelation concepts[1][2]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Practice Tasks:**\n",
    "- Calculate Bitcoin's daily returns and volatility[11][12][6]\n",
    "- Compute rolling statistics (7-day, 30-day moving averages)[10][7]\n",
    "- Identify correlation between different cryptocurrencies[13][14]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Formulas:**\n",
    "- Daily Return: $$\\text{Return}_t = \\frac{\\text{Price}_t - \\text{Price}_{t-1}}{\\text{Price}_{t-1}}$$[6]\n",
    "- Volatility (Standard Deviation): $$\\sigma = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N}(x_i - \\mu)^2}$$[6]\n",
    "\n",
    "***\n",
    "\n",
    "## Phase 2: Core Time Series Concepts (Weeks 5-8)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 5-6: Time Series Components & Stationarity\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to Learn:**\n",
    "- Trend, Seasonality, Cyclic patterns, and Residuals[1][3][2]\n",
    "- Stationarity concept and why it matters[15][1][2]\n",
    "- Augmented Dickey-Fuller (ADF) test for unit root testing[16][15][1]\n",
    "- KPSS test for stationarity verification[16]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Practice Tasks:**\n",
    "- Decompose Bitcoin price into trend, seasonal, and residual components using `seasonal_decompose()`[3][2]\n",
    "- Perform ADF test on crypto prices to check stationarity[12][11][15]\n",
    "- Apply differencing to make non-stationary data stationary[10][1][2]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Code Example:**\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from statsmodels.tsa.stattools import adfuller\n",
    "from statsmodels.tsa.seasonal import seasonal_decompose\n",
    "\n",
    "# ADF Test\n",
    "result = adfuller(crypto_prices['Close'])\n",
    "print(f'ADF Statistic: {result[0]}')\n",
    "print(f'p-value: {result[1]}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Decomposition\n",
    "decomposition = seasonal_decompose(crypto_prices['Close'], model='multiplicative', period=30)\n",
    "decomposition.plot()\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why It Matters:**\n",
    "Crypto prices are highly non-stationary due to volatility. Most classical models (ARIMA) require stationary data.[11][12][1]\n",
    "\n",
    "***\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 7-8: Feature Engineering for Time Series\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to Learn:**\n",
    "- Lag features (previous day's price, week's price)[17][7][10]\n",
    "- Rolling window statistics (moving averages, rolling std)[18][9][7]\n",
    "- Time-based features (day of week, month, quarter, holidays)[19][9][7]\n",
    "- Technical indicators (RSI, MACD, EMA, Bollinger Bands)[20][6]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Practice Tasks:**\n",
    "- Create lag features for 1, 7, 30 days[7][10]\n",
    "- Calculate 20-day and 50-day Exponential Moving Averages (EMA)[6]\n",
    "- Compute RSI (Relative Strength Index) and MACD indicators[6]\n",
    "- Extract cyclical features using sine/cosine transformations for time of day[9][19]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Code Example:**\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# Lag Features\n",
    "df['lag_1'] = df['Close'].shift(1)\n",
    "df['lag_7'] = df['Close'].shift(7)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Rolling Statistics\n",
    "df['rolling_mean_30'] = df['Close'].rolling(window=30).mean()\n",
    "df['rolling_std_30'] = df['Close'].rolling(window=30).std()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Technical Indicators\n",
    "def calculate_rsi(data, period=14):\n",
    "    delta = data.diff()\n",
    "    gain = (delta.where(delta > 0, 0)).rolling(window=period).mean()\n",
    "    loss = (-delta.where(delta < 0, 0)).rolling(window=period).mean()\n",
    "    rs = gain / loss\n",
    "    return 100 - (100 / (1 + rs))\n",
    "\n",
    "df['RSI'] = calculate_rsi(df['Close'])\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "***\n",
    "\n",
    "## Phase 3: Traditional Statistical Models (Weeks 9-12)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 9-10: ARIMA Models\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to Learn:**\n",
    "- AR (AutoRegressive) component: past values predict future[12][11][1]\n",
    "- I (Integrated) component: differencing for stationarity[1][2]\n",
    "- MA (Moving Average) component: past forecast errors[11][1]\n",
    "- ACF (Autocorrelation Function) and PACF (Partial Autocorrelation Function) plots[21][2][3]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Practice Tasks:**\n",
    "- Plot ACF and PACF to determine ARIMA parameters (p, d, q)[3][1]\n",
    "- Build ARIMA model for Bitcoin price prediction[22][12][11]\n",
    "- Use `auto_arima` for automatic parameter selection[12]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Code Example:**\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from statsmodels.tsa.arima.model import ARIMA\n",
    "from pmdarima import auto_arima\n",
    "\n",
    "# Auto ARIMA\n",
    "model = auto_arima(crypto_prices['Close'], seasonal=False, trace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Manual ARIMA\n",
    "arima_model = ARIMA(crypto_prices['Close'], order=(5,1,2))\n",
    "fitted_model = arima_model.fit()\n",
    "predictions = fitted_model.forecast(steps=30)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**When to Use:**\n",
    "Good for short-term predictions on relatively stable crypto assets. Not ideal for highly volatile assets like meme coins.[23][11][12]\n",
    "\n",
    "***\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 11-12: SARIMA & Prophet\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to Learn:**\n",
    "- SARIMA: Seasonal ARIMA for data with seasonal patterns[8][3]\n",
    "- Facebook Prophet: Additive model with trend, seasonality, and holidays[24][25][26][27]\n",
    "- Prophet's changepoint detection for trend shifts[27]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Practice Tasks:**\n",
    "- Implement SARIMA for crypto with weekly/monthly patterns[28][3]\n",
    "- Use Prophet to forecast Bitcoin with automatic seasonality detection[25][29][24]\n",
    "- Add custom holidays/events (Bitcoin halvings, major announcements)[25]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Code Example:**\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from fbprophet import Prophet\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare data for Prophet\n",
    "df_prophet = crypto_prices.reset_index()\n",
    "df_prophet.columns = ['ds', 'y']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train Prophet model\n",
    "model = Prophet(daily_seasonality=True, weekly_seasonality=True)\n",
    "model.fit(df_prophet)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Make predictions\n",
    "future = model.make_future_dataframe(periods=30)\n",
    "forecast = model.predict(future)\n",
    "model.plot(forecast)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Advantages:**\n",
    "Prophet handles missing data well and automatically detects changepoints (trend reversals).[24][27]\n",
    "\n",
    "***\n",
    "\n",
    "## Phase 4: Machine Learning Models (Weeks 13-16)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 13-14: Tree-Based Models\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to Learn:**\n",
    "- Random Forest for time series regression[30][23]\n",
    "- XGBoost (Extreme Gradient Boosting) for crypto prediction[20][11][12][6]\n",
    "- Feature importance analysis[20][6]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Practice Tasks:**\n",
    "- Engineer features (lags, rolling stats, technical indicators)[20][6]\n",
    "- Train XGBoost regressor on Bitcoin with hyperparameter tuning[31][6][20]\n",
    "- Evaluate model using MAE, RMSE, R²[11][12][6]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Code Example:**\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from xgboost import XGBRegressor\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import TimeSeriesSplit\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error\n",
    "\n",
    "# Feature engineering\n",
    "features = ['lag_1', 'lag_7', 'rolling_mean_30', 'RSI', 'MACD']\n",
    "X = df[features]\n",
    "y = df['Close']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Time series split (no shuffling)\n",
    "tscv = TimeSeriesSplit(n_splits=5)\n",
    "\n",
    "# XGBoost model\n",
    "model = XGBRegressor(n_estimators=1000, learning_rate=0.01, max_depth=5)\n",
    "model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predictions\n",
    "predictions = model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, predictions))\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why It Works:**\n",
    "XGBoost captures non-linear relationships and handles high-dimensional feature spaces well.[32][6][20]\n",
    "\n",
    "***\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 15-16: Ensemble & Hybrid Models\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to Learn:**\n",
    "- Combining ARIMA + LSTM for hybrid predictions[33][34]\n",
    "- Ensemble methods (averaging, stacking, voting)[35]\n",
    "- Model blending strategies[35]\n",
    "\n",
